            "text": "The reproduction confirms both failures. I’ll use one path for every write: store the value, move the key to the most-recent end, then evict the oldest entry if capacity is exceeded. This removes the truthiness-dependent behavior; I’ll also correct the ordering description in the docstring.\n"
          }
        ],
        "phase": "commentary",
        "role": "assistant"
      },
      {
        "id": "fc_0987994f4d9abe7e016ae65faa95a48193b6eefde84616df00",
        "type": "function_call",
        "status": "completed",
        "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cd /testbed && python - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\npath = Path('tinydb/utils.py')\\nsource = path.read_text()\\nold_doc = '''    This is implemented using an ``OrderedDict``. On every access the accessed\\n    entry is moved to the front by re-inserting it into the ``OrderedDict``.\\n    When adding an entry and the cache size is exceeded, the last entry will\\n    be discarded.\\n'''\\nnew_doc = '''    This is implemented using an ``OrderedDict``. On every read or write, the\\n    accessed entry is moved to the end of the ``OrderedDict``. When adding an\\n    entry and the cache size is exceeded, the first (least recently used) entry\\n    will be discarded.\\n'''\\nold_set = '''    def set(self, key: K, value: V):\\n        if self.cache.get(key):\\n            self.cache[key] = value\\n\\n            # Check, if the cache is full and we have to remove old items\\n            # If the queue is of unlimited size, self.capacity is NaN and\\n            # x > NaN is always False in Python and the cache won't be cleared.\\n            if self.capacity is not None and self.length > self.capacity:\\n                self.cache.popitem(last=False)\\n        else:\\n            self.cache[key] = value\\n            self.cache.move_to_end(key, last=True)\\n\\nclass FrozenDict(dict):\\n'''\\nnew_set = '''    def set(self, key: K, value: V) -> None:\\n        self.cache[key] = value\\n        self.cache.move_to_end(key, last=True)\\n\\n        # Evict the least recently used item if the cache exceeds its capacity.\\n        # A capacity of None means the cache is unlimited.\\n        if self.capacity is not None and self.length > self.capacity:\\n            self.cache.popitem(last=False)\\n\\n\\nclass FrozenDict(dict):\\n'''\\nassert source.count(old_doc) == 1\\nassert source.count(old_set) == 1\\npath.write_text(source.replace(old_doc, new_doc).replace(old_set, new_set))\\nPY\\nprintf '\\\\n--- reproduction after fix ---\\\\n' && PYTHONPATH=/testbed python /tmp/tinydb_lru_repro.py && printf '\\\\n--- cache and table tests ---\\\\n' && python -m pytest tests/test_utils.py tests/test_tables.py -q -o addopts='' && printf '\\\\n--- patch review ---\\\\n' && git diff --check && git diff --stat && git diff -- tinydb/utils.py tests/test_utils.py tests/test_tables.py\"}",
        "call_id": "call_HLuppbgNds5EPOILGPPxofzz",
        "name": "bash"
      }
